{
  "family": "parsec",
  "channel": "form",
  "ca_bundle": "ZeroSSLRSADVSSLCA2.crt",
  "source_note": "PARSEC publishes no isochrone packages: the official CMD web form (https://stev.oapd.inaf.it/cgi-bin/cmd) computes isochrone tables server-side on request and is the isochrone acquisition channel (scriptable with a complete current field set, verified live 2026-10-14; complete wire documentation: docs/parsec/cmd-form.md). The host's TLS chain omits its intermediate CA (ZeroSSL RSA DV SSL CA 2); the bundled intermediate completes the chain so verification stays on.",
  "scope_note": "Registry of the form-computed products still archived in the reference database (request-layer client: stellariso.models.parsec.cmd_form): the two primary track sets at their full [M/H] extent on a 0.1 dex grid, one fine-step log-age table per composition - each product is the log-age half of a blueprint cell. The coarse-grid secondary products and one-shot option-variation tables of the 2026-10-15/16 fetch were pruned on 2026-10-16, when the blueprint redesign disowned them; their exact payloads remain in this file's git history. The declared acquisition design - the full cell space the build completes towards, secondary sets and all axes included - lives in stellariso.models.parsec.blueprint (docs/parsec/blueprint.md). Historical pre-2006 tracks on pleiadi.oapd.inaf.it remain out of scope.",
  "matrix_notes": {
    "ages": "log10(age/yr) 6.6-10.13 at the fine step 0.02 dex (~177 ages per composition); the linear young-age half of each cell is a blueprint-builder acquisition archived beside the log table",
    "metallicities": "one product per [M/H] on a 0.1 dex grid (single-value jobs; range end points are unreliable server-side)",
    "photometry": "placeholder only: YBC UBVRIJHK for the YBC-served sets (the archived pairs both are)",
    "extinction": "A_V = 0 everywhere; extinction changes magnitudes only (verified 2026-10-15, docs/parsec/cmd-form.md)",
    "archived_options": "the archived products keep circumstellar dust, the LPV prescription, Reimers eta, and the TP-cycle resolution at their canonical values; the blueprint declares them as designed cell axes"
  },
